' Guide - how a sprite is loaded with Coil (explanatory diagram for the root README)
' Version 1.0 - 2026-10-19 - reflects the current working tree
' The app uses Coil's default singleton ImageLoader (no custom configuration in the code); the cache steps are
' Coil 3's default behaviour. Network access comes from coil-network-okhttp.
' Sprite URLs: PokemonSummary.spriteUrl (list cards, evolution stages) is built from the Pokédex number by spriteUrlFor()
' (raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites); the detail screen uses the URLs inside the PokeAPI response.
@startuml coil-image-loading
!include ../style.puml

title Coil - loading a Pokémon sprite

start
:Composable calls **AsyncImage**(model = sprite URL);
:Coil's default ImageLoader builds the request;
if (In memory cache?) then (yes)
else (no)
  if (In disk cache?) then (yes)
  else (no)
    :Download with OkHttp
    (PokeAPI Sprites, GitHub raw);
    :Save to disk cache;
  endif
  :Decode into a bitmap;
  :Keep it in memory cache;
endif
:Compose draws it with ContentScale.Fit
(FilterQuality.None on the detail screen
keeps the pixel art sharp);
stop
@enduml
